\description{
The \code{MzTabM()} method for the \link[SummarizedExperiment:SummarizedExperiment]{SummarizedExperiment::SummarizedExperiment}
class compiles a \link{MzTabM} data object from the content and data of the
\code{SummarizedExperiment} object passed through the function's first parameter
(\code{mtd}). The function extracts relevant information from the
\code{SummarizedExperiment}'s \code{rowData()} and \code{colData()}. The
\code{SummarizedExperiment}'s \code{rowData()} is expected to contain necessary
information to characterize the individual features. The \code{colData()} should
provide experiment and sample information for the mzTab-M metadata section.
\code{MzTabM()} uses the \code{\link[=mtdFromSampleData]{mtdFromSampleData()}} and \code{smf()} method (described
below) to compile the mzTab-M's MTD and SMF sections, respectively.
\itemize{
\item \strong{MTD} section: information is extracted from the \code{SummarizedExperiment}'s
\code{colData()}. If not already present, relevant and required information
should be added to the \code{colData()}. The \code{\link[=mtdFromSampleData]{mtdFromSampleData()}} function is
used to extract and compile the MTD section.
\item \strong{SMF} section: the small molecule feature section is compiled from the
\code{SummarizedExperiment}'s \code{rowData()} (for feature characteristics) and
\code{assay()} (abundance matrix). The \code{smfCols.} parameter of the \code{smf()} and
\code{MzTabM()} methods allows to define the mapping between feature \emph{fields}
and column names of the \code{rowData()} containing the relevant information.
}

\code{makeSummarizedExperimentFromMzTabM} converts the content of an \code{MzTabM}
object into a \code{SummarizedExperiment} object. Sample information is extracted
from the \emph{MTD} (metadata) section and used to populate the \code{colData} of the
resulting object, while feature-level quantification values and feature
annotations are extracted from the \emph{SMF} section and used to populate the
assay data and \code{rowData}, respectively.
If the \code{MzTabM} object does not contain any small molecule feature data, a
\code{SummarizedExperiment} with only \code{colData} populated is returned.
}
